    {
      "candidate": "REKR 2026-07-15",
      "question": "Exclude it as a preliminary pre-announcement?",
      "finding": "The 8-K says the release announces certain preliminary, unaudited financial results, with an outlook and a product launch; the full second-quarter results followed on 2026-08-13 (REKR 2026-08-13 is in the pool).",
      "recommendation": "Exclude, as steps 2 and 3 did for Rekor's earlier pre-announcements (not a qualifying earnings event)."
    },
    {
      "candidate": "ASMB 2026-08-14",
      "question": "Keep the 8-K/A as the pool's representation of the 2026-08-13 results release, or exclude it as an amendment?",
      "finding": "It only corrects the submission header of the 2026-08-13 8-K (Item 2.02 had been tagged as Item 2.01); the release is dated 2026-08-13. The original 8-K is not in the pool, so excluding the amendment, as step 3 did for CACI's 8-K/A (there the original was a candidate), would leave that release out.",
      "recommendation": "Keep it, with a caveat, and take the release's first-public time from the 2026-08-13 wire and 8-K (EDGAR accepted the original at 16:11 ET that day, so the release was public by then), not from 2026-08-14. Excluding it is the literal reading of the step 3 rule and costs one event."
    },
    {
      "candidate": "PAYO 2026-08-06",
      "question": "Exclude it because the security was under a pending cash take-private?",
      "finding": "On 2026-06-15 Payoneer agreed to be acquired by Nuvei for $7.40 per share in cash (about $2.75 billion), closing expected in mid-2027; the release suspends earnings calls and guidance and withdraws the 2026 outlook. Its earlier release, PAYO 2026-05-07, predates the deal.",
      "recommendation": "Exclude: a price pinned to a cash offer is not an earnings reaction, and this is a new category that steps 2 and 3 did not meet, so it needs the owner's word."
    }
